  "visualFindings": {
    "identity": "Rose-red adult-male head/chest, stout conical bill and brown/buff wing-tail pattern remain recognizably House Finch. New drawings have a larger, fuller head/body presentation than the selected individual; species readability does not establish individual/scale continuity.",
    "actualPoseChanges": "Native sheet and actual96CSS output show a low compression stance, curled/tucked feet off the belly, forward-reaching extended toes/legs, and a low supported-intent settle. These are four actual source drawings with changed leg/body arrangements, not wholebody translation credited as new art. Compression and settle are related quiet low-posture categories; no biological phase completeness inferred.",
    "entryReturnScale": "At normal light/dark presentation, exact awake to compression visibly grows and shifts the entire bird, beyond a modest crouch silhouette change. The new family remains enlarged; settle to old awake reverses the enlargement at tick18. Tail, head, wing mass and foot placement all contribute. Visible widths49 to73/72/74/72world corroborate this direct observation; bbox equality is not a universal quality gate.",
    "stanceAndGround": "At unchanged nominal planted root, compression feet extend visibly below the diagnostic ground line; supported-intent settle also sits below it, then the old awake return changes the apparent foot plane. At the airborne key switch, image-native body/foot placement adds a visible vertical pop over the small authored arc. Empty new contacts and supportWorldnull are appropriate. Positive source toe pixels/probes do not establish soles, loaded pressure, bilateral support or toe lock.",
    "anatomy": "Distinct curled versus extended digits are visible; crowded claw/toe overlaps and tiny raster feet prevent confident left/right toe ownership or load assessment. No independent anatomical support acceptance is given. Native feet inspected enlarged as well as output96; intended air/ground labels are not physical proof.",
    "alphaAndStyle": "Soft alpha and red partial-alpha edge pixels are retained unchanged. Native black-backed view exposes red fringe, but normal light/dark composites do not make a conspicuous opaque red outline the primary defect. Minor feather-edge shimmer remains; dominant rejection is visible scale/placement/ground discontinuity, not a numerical color or outside-body-pixel gate.",
    "normalSpeed": "Authored one-second sequence reads as stepped large posture swaps and a reset to the smaller source individual, rather than a coherent matched hop. Ground-intent root stations are necessary but cannot hold actual toes when source placement changes. It is not a walk, validated full locomotion or smooth biological motion."
  },
